aak-marketing — additional third-party sources
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Many skills, agents, and workflows in `plugins/aak-marketing/` are adapted from
the following upstream projects. Each is credited here; their license terms
apply to the adapted portions.

- antigravity-marketing (https://github.com/nguyenphp/antigravity-marketing),
  Copyright (c) NguyenPHP, MIT (as declared in the project's package.json and
  README). Source of most marketing skills, the 4 marketing agents, and the
  /campaign, /content, /optimize, /analyze, /report, /brand-report workflows.
  Includes the `vision-analysis` skill, re-pointed from the paid MiniMax vision
  tool to Claude's native image reading (MiniMax kept as an optional fallback).

- ClaudeKit (https://claudekit.cc / https://github.com/mrgoonie/claudekit-skills),
  by claudekit. Source of the `brand` and `banner-design` skills. Both were
  adapted to run standalone (the `brand` token-sync script was made
  self-contained; `banner-design` image/screenshot steps were repointed to
  available image-generation and browser tools).

- MiniMax-AI/skills (https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/skills), Copyright (c) 2026
  MiniMax, MIT. Source of the `minimax-pdf` skill (styled, local PDF generation).

- Remotion Dev Skills (https://github.com/remotion-dev/skills), by Remotion.
  Source of `remotion-best-practices`, `video-automation`, `tutorial-video-expert`.

- vibeship-spawner-skills, Apache License 2.0. Source of the
  `viral-generator-builder` skill. Under Apache-2.0, this notice preserves the
  attribution; see the upstream project for the full license text.

- Antigravity Awesome Skills (https://github.com/sickn33/antigravity-awesome-skills),
  community-contributed. Origin of several patterns (e.g. `marketing-ideas`,
  the CRO-suite skills, `programmatic-seo`) as bundled via antigravity-marketing.

- ai-marketing-claude (https://github.com/zubair-trabzada/ai-marketing-claude),
  Copyright (c) 2026 Zubair Trabzada, MIT. Source of: the `client-proposal` skill
  and its proposal template; the email/content/launch templates bundled under
  `email-marketing`, `content-marketing`, and `launch-strategy`; the verbatim
  scoring rubrics, weights, and report format in the `site-audit` skill (its five
  audit-dimension rubric files are copied from that project's audit subagents); and
  `site-audit/scripts/analyze_page.py` (parsing/scoring logic unchanged; a
  network-safety wrapper was added in front of the fetchers). The `/audit` command
  wires these to this kit's own marketing agents rather than vendoring theirs.

- vietnamese-language-skill (https://github.com/trussary/vietnamese-language-skill),
  Copyright (c) trussary, MIT. Vendored verbatim as the `aak-vietnamese` plugin —
  the five `vietnamese-*` skills (SKILL.md bodies, references, and the dependency-free
  `validate_copy.py` linter + domain `rules_*.py`), the shared references, and the eval
  corpus, all byte-identical to pinned commit
  1c44546d7862e0d09491a2a711a64086ab8c80d7 (2026-08-22). Only `plugin.json`
  identity fields (name/author/homepage/repository) were changed; a non-vendored
  acceptance harness (`.acceptance/replay_evals.py`) was added by this project.

Where an upstream skill shipped a placeholder/stub library (marketing-ideas,
marketing-psychology), the missing content was authored fresh for this project.
